
Usage:
      Compress: press -c <archive file> [<options>] [<file to compress>...]
      Archive:  press -a <archive file> [<options>] [<file to archive>...]
      Extract:  press -x <archive file> [<options>] [<file to extract>...]
      Print:    press -p <archive file> [<options>] [<file to print>...]
      List:     press -l <archive file> [<options>] [<file to list>...]
      Delete:   press -d <archive file> [<options>] <file to delete>...

      Help:     press         (prints this message)
      More help:press -h      (prints more details)

      -c  perform compression into <archive file>
      -a  add file(s) to <archive file> in uncompressed format
      -x  extract (& decompress) file(s) from <archive file>
      -p  extract (& decompress) from <archive file> to standard output
      -l  list file names in <archive file>
      -d  delete file(s) from <archive file>
          (produces new file -- old file saved with ".bak" suffix)

      Options:
      -q  work quietly
      -t  text file(s) (retrieves with correct line end format)
	-n  process all files in archive *except* specified files

      LZW Experimentor Options:
      -T  produce detailed compression trace info (to standard error file)
      -S  maximum compression string table size
          (for -c only -- default = 1024)

status 1
